extraction_notes: |
  - NPC-headed entry that is also an optional player R.C.C.: the stat block is headed "Darkhound - NPC Villain & Optional Player R.C.C." (printed 97) and carries a Player Character Note on playing it; imported as a playable race on that basis.
  - xp_table: the book disagrees with itself. The class page (printed 97) says to use the Juicer''s experience table; the book''s own Experience Tables page (printed 157) lists the Darkhound on the Psi-Druid / Psi-Ghost / Darkhound ladder. The printed-157 table is the book''s authority for ladders, so that is the stored xp_table; the Juicer line is recorded here as the losing reading.
  - No O.C.C. pairing is stated either way, so no occ_restrictions is written; the R.C.C. skills plus four secondary skills are the whole skill grant (printed 97). Related skills: none, correct for an R.C.C.
  - Secondary skills: the book limits them to Physical (any), Technical (spoken language and lore skills only) and Wilderness (any). Recorded in the secondary_skills note rather than as a category list, because the Technical limit is a name family (Language: / Lore:) that an only-list would have to enumerate and re-enumerate.
  - Psionics as printed in Special Abilities #4 (printed 96): Sense Evil, Sense Magic, Deaden Senses, Nightvision, Resist Fatigue, Empathy (receiver only, not transmission), plus one additional Sensitive power. The book does NOT list Sixth Sense here, unlike the Dog Boy; transcribed as printed. Master Psychic, saves vs psionics at 10 or higher (#6).
  - I.S.P. (#5): 1D6x10 + M.E., +10 per additional level; regained 2 per hour of activity or 12 per hour of meditation or sleep. P.P.E. (#7): permanent base 2D6.
  - Bonuses (#8, printed 96): +2 initiative at levels 1, 4, 8 and 14; +1 attack at levels 1, 5 and 10; +1 strike, +3 pull punch, +1 roll, +4 save vs Horror Factor, +3 save vs disease and poison (stored as disease and toxins_poisons), +2 save vs possession.
  - Horror Factor 11 stored; the 14 against supernatural creatures and magic practitioners is conditional and stays in side_effects.
  - M.D.C.: 3D6x10 plus 2D6 per level (printed 97). A former Dog Boy "begins life anew" as a Darkhound; nothing to store.
  - Armor: about half fashion partial body armor from scraps (two thirds of those prefer Coalition armor), typically 1D4x10+15 M.D.C. (printed 95). Not given as starting gear because the book makes it a 50% chance; recorded in GM Notes.
  - Equipment (printed 98): "one Vibro-Blade and a knife". The book names no specific Vibro-Blade, so it is a choice among the generic vibro-knife, vibro-saber and vibro-sword rows. Money: none, so no starting_money. Ragged clothing is not stored.
  - Damage: claws 2D6 M.D. + supernatural P.S. damage, bite 4D6 M.D. (printed 97), recorded as a natural ability.
  - Cache digit faults: "!D6xlO" (I.S.P., p097) read as 1D6x10, "3D6xlO" (M.D.C., p098) as 3D6x10, "!D4xlO+15" (armor, p096) as 1D4x10+15, per the brief''s known fault list.
